    "updated_at": "2026-11-03T17:06:25Z",
    "body": "The latest instant that finally got me to write this down, was https://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues/1539 which describes a common pattern that would be solved by `<th scope=rowgroup colspan=auto>` (and usually also by `0`), while some authors would prefer `rowspan` in similar cases. \n\nOver the years, I’ve seen (and sometimes debugged) many tables that tried to span a cell across a certain set of columns or rows, but got the number wrong by &pm;1 or more, often due to subsequent, collaborative editing, e.g. at Wikipedia. I did not take notes, unfortunately. I’ve hardly seen authors asking for a better alternative, often – I believe – because they didn’t even realize there was a problem. \n\nSomeone with access to a large archive website could examine how often `rowspan=0` is used in the wild, which probably is not that much at all. My assumption is that this would be due to missing knowledge more than to missing need. ",
